                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Ziggy's Chase is a primitive 3D platformer, the closest comparison that I can come up with is the old reboot Frogger games. There's a functional product here with a core gameplay loop. It's an adequate game by mobile game standards, nothing outright offensive. But I didn't have a damn bit of fun playing it. The mechanics are clunky and simplistic, repetition kicked in for me within a few stages, level design is boring. Visually the game is adequate but uninteresting. It's okay. It's definitely not the worst game in existence. But it's fundamentally a time waster and you're not missing out on anything by not playing.",
